<title>BRAZIL: FORECAST - Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Consensus survey of Brazilian indicators.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are consensus forecasts from a Reuter survey of Brazilian economic indicators taken from eight Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro brokerages and research firms. Also included are current market rates for dollar and interest rate futures over the next three months.</p>
<p>Each are updated twice monthly, normally in the second and fourth weeks of each month.</p>
<p>  Exports	     March     $3.694 bln  $3.652 bln   N.A.</p>
<p>  Imports	     March     $4.669 bln  $4.608 bln   N.A.</p>
<p>				*****</p>
<p>	     Brazilian Financial Indicators</p>
<p>	  Futures market rates at March 26 Close</p>
<p>			  April	     May	     June</p>
<p>Real/Dollar	  1.0675	    1.0740	  1.0824</p>
<p>Monthly Int Rates  1.609  pct	1.581  pct    1.570 pct</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Notes - Price indicators reflect monthly variation. Industrial activity reflects annual variation.</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>****Brazil Indicators - March Consensus Forecast****</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>  INDICATOR	   PERIOD    AVG FORCST   MEDIAN	PRVS MONTH</p>
<p>  CPI (Fipe)	  March     0.25   pct  0.28   pct   0.01   pct</p>
<p>  PPI (IPA-M/FGV)   March     1.46   pct  1.50   pct   0.27   pct</p>
<p>  Inflation (IGP-M) March     1.07   pct  1.10   pct   0.43   pct</p>
<p>  Ind Act (IBGE)     Feb	4.90   pct  5.19   pct   6.70   pct</p>
<p>  Trade Balance     March    -$977   million -$994   million   N.A</p>
<p>((--John Miller, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248-5414))</p>
